&lt;p&gt;    this &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2695#issuecomment-349882841&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2695#issuecomment-349882841&lt;/a&gt; is a good point...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16287233" author="githubbot" created="Tue, 12 Dec 2017 07:45:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user yu74n commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2695&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2695&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Whether a user can find the notebook in trash or not is based on permission of the notebook, then If user &apos;B&apos; has properly permission for the notebook deleted by user &apos;A&apos;, user &apos;B&apos; can find the notebook in trash.&lt;br/&gt;
    However, I find some issues in this PR. For example, user &apos;A&apos; delete a notebook, then user &apos;B&apos; restore the notebook from trash. In this PR, even if user &apos;B&apos; has &apos;owner&apos; permission for the notebook, cannot do that.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
